# netsurf: precise sibling-combinator decline for block insert/remove (166 follow-up, WS-C)
# Generated 2026-10-02
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser ebbacb5637d7eadd8df802d214d4b7143b009a1f (patch stack through 197)
#
# What remains of the patch-166 stale-styles issue after 192 and 197:
# inserting or removing a block among a parent's block children can change
# a FOLLOWING sibling's style through a sibling combinator (+ / ~), flip
# the parent's :empty, or change an ancestor's :has() answer, and the
# local block path never reselects the siblings, the parent or the
# ancestors -- their styles go stale. Patch 192 covers positional
# pseudos and counters; 197 covers class changes on the element itself.
# Shelved 189 declined ANY insert/remove under a sibling-combinator
# sheet, which over-declined (DOMSTALL 1185-1670 ms against the 200 ms
# bound), so this patch is precise per element instead.
#
# Fix: patch 186's per-sheet selector analysis now records, alongside
# lefts[] (unchanged), the sibling rules {kind '+'/'~', L, R} -- including
# chained A + B + C -- and the compounds carrying :empty / :has().
# html_rl_block_change calls html_rl_block_sibling_risk after 192's
# structural check, before any box is touched:
#   '+' : the next sibling S of the inserted/removed element changes iff
#         R matches S and L's match differs between the old and the new
#         predecessor. Compared per element.
#   '~' : any following sibling matching R changes iff the
#         inserted/removed element matches L.
#   :empty : the parent's :empty flips iff the mutation changes its
#         element-childlessness, and an :empty compound statically
#         matches the parent.
#   :has : an insert/remove below changes the answer of a :has()
#         compound statically matching the parent or any ancestor.
# A sheet in patch 186's conservative state (2) still declines. The
# DOMSTALL inserts stay local: their sheets carry no matching + / ~
# compound and the span:empty parent is not :empty-matched, so the
# 5000-paragraph pages keep their local rebuilds.
#
# Companion fix (shared scanner): html_rl_skip_ws now strips CSS
# comments. Before this, a comment inside a selector prelude (e.g. the
# note above DOMSTALL's "span:empty { ... }") made the parser fail on
# the '/' and the whole sheet fell into the conservative decline state
# even though it carries no sibling risk -- which would have forced
# every insert on such a page through the full rebuild. Comments may
# sit between any two tokens in CSS, so the tokeniser now treats them
# as whitespace everywhere it skips. This also sharpens patch 186's
# class-path analysis for the same sheets.
#
# Logging: "LIFE rebuild local: declined (sibling combinator may
# restyle on insert/remove)"; the gate counts it (>= 2) and the
# JS-block-sibling-insert page asserts the following sibling's computed
# colour actually changed (on the unstaled local path it would not).
#
# Decline conditions: as above, plus any DOM error while walking (the
# check cannot prove safety). Chained selectors (A + B + C) yield both
# rules; the class-change XOR in 186 is untouched.
